1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,911
Founder updates can help
investors follow progress, but an

2
00:00:03,911 --> 00:00:08,025
update is not a guarantee and
may not be audited or complete.

3
00:00:08,025 --> 00:00:12,446
Look for a consistent time period
and metrics that connect to the

4
00:00:12,446 --> 00:00:16,527
business plan: paying customers,
revenue, retention, product

5
00:00:16,527 --> 00:00:18,500
milestones, cash, and hiring.

6
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:20,628
Compare the update with earlier

7
00:00:20,628 --> 00:00:22,962
disclosures and note what
changed.

8
00:00:22,962 --> 00:00:27,725
Ask whether numbers are actual
results, forecasts, or goals.

9
00:00:27,725 --> 00:00:32,650
In Reg CF, issuers generally have
annual reporting obligations, with

10
00:00:32,650 --> 00:00:37,357
exceptions and specific rules; an
informal monthly email is not a

11
00:00:37,357 --> 00:00:39,675
substitute for required filings.

12
00:00:39,675 --> 00:00:45,129
For example, a fictional company
might report 250 customers last

13
00:00:45,129 --> 00:00:47,600
quarter and 325 this quarter.

14
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:52,719
That is an increase of 75, or 30%,
but it does not show revenue per

15
00:00:52,719 --> 00:00:57,150
customer, churn, profitability, or
whether customers paid.

16
00:00:57,150 --> 00:01:01,754
Watch for clear explanations of
setbacks and revised plans, not

17
00:01:01,754 --> 00:01:03,800
only celebratory highlights.

18
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:06,154
Keep copies of updates and filings

19
00:01:06,154 --> 00:01:08,784
so you can compare progress
over time.

